+# VSG-2B-TEXT-SERIALIZED-AB-1
+
+This contract limits any result to a comparison of two textual serializations of
+identical frozen scene constraints in the provider's prompt string. It does not
+measure a native typed-array interface or establish a native structured-input gain.
+
+A: canonical JSON of the entire existing payload, retaining relations_and_locks as
+its original JSON-lines string. B: canonical JSON of the entire existing payload,
+retaining relations_and_locks as an array inside that text. Serialize with
+json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False,
+allow_nan=False), UTF-8, without prefix, suffix or trailing newline. Preserve all
+array order, IDs, priorities, locks, common content and prohibitions. Do not parse
+A into an array before serialization. Do not truncate, summarize, pad or add hidden
+instructions to either branch. Provider prompt upsampling is false in both.
+
+The source remains its original JPEG bytes in an in-memory data URI. Both requests
+must use the same pinned model, explicit seed, aspect policy, format and safety
+setting. No retries, local cropping, resizing, compression, postprocessing or other
+branch-specific transformation is permitted. Pin the serializer implementation,
+provider version and parameters and bind exact provider-body hashes into the new
+delta review; the legacy manifest-plus-payload delta alone cannot bind a new bridge.
+
+Visual rubric: retain every original source-relative criterion, region, severity,
+priority, identity and unauthorized-change rule. Keep branch identity, prompts and
+provider settings hidden from the independent reviewer. Findings still score images
+against the source. Technical JSON equality or prediction IDs are not visual scores.
+S3, protected loss, regression, UNKNOWN, uncontrolled seed and STOP keep blocking.
+
+Interpretation rubric: an improvement may only be reported as an improvement for
+TEXT_SERIALIZED_AB under the pinned configuration. Prompt length and escaping differ
+and are part of this treatment; do not attribute outcomes to a native array API.
+All reports must carry this experiment ID and native_structured_evidence=false.
+
+Campaign scope stays D/E/Kenny/C, four distinct representative fixtures and eight
+attempts maximum; Reference Isolation remains mandatory and C remains blocked.
+A later operational migration may replace the D representative with R2B-191-D-P1,
+preserving the old fixture/admission for K1. Old D plus new D must never count as
+two representatives or permit a second D attempt under a different ID. F does not
+replace C. production_authorized remains false.
+
+Before admission, require exact version availability and pin semantics, full-length
+prompt acceptance and truncation behavior, source data-URI support, reproducible
+seed semantics, safe receipt attribution, a tested provider bridge, coherent
+manifest/policy/schema migration, fresh preconditions and a newly reviewed delta.
+Approval of this scope contract does not authorize a prediction or spend image calls.
